From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pravalika Gurram <pravalika.gurram@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe: Restore PCI devres state on resume

Until 77f79ac8de0f ("PCI: Remove struct pci_devres.enabled status
bit"), pci_disable_device() clears the PCI core's "enabled" flag and
only pcim_enable_device() sets it again. xe uses pci_enable_device() on
resume, so the flag stays cleared. On unbind the PCI core then skips the
final disable and the enable count leaks.

On the next probe the device is not powered up. A PF still works as it
has a PM capability to recover D0 from, but its enable count keeps
leaking. A VF has no PM capability, so IRQ allocation fails with
-EINVAL.

Use pcim_enable_device() on resume so the flag is set again.

Signed-off-by: Pravalika Gurram <pravalika.gurram@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci.c
index 5f2a0b1..cd650f0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci.c
@@ -1347,7 +1347,11 @@ static int xe_pci_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	pci_restore_state(pdev);
 
-	err = pci_enable_device(pdev);
+#ifdef BPM_PCI_DEVRES_ENABLED_PRESENT
+	err = pcim_enable_device(pdev);
+#else
+	err = pci_enable_device(pdev);
+#endif
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
@@ -1411,7 +1415,11 @@ static int xe_pci_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	pci_restore_state(pdev);
 
 	if (xe->d3cold.allowed) {
-		err = pci_enable_device(pdev);
+#ifdef BPM_PCI_DEVRES_ENABLED_PRESENT
+		err = pcim_enable_device(pdev);
+#else
+		err = pci_enable_device(pdev);
+#endif
 		if (err)
 			return err;
 
